# For LOCAL DEVELOPMENT only: copy this file to ".dev.vars" in the repo ROOT
# (`cp docs/dev.vars.example .dev.vars`) for `wrangler dev`.
# For production, set the SAME names as Worker secrets:  wrangler secret put NAME
# NEVER commit a file with real values — .dev.vars is gitignored.
#
# Why does this live in docs/ and not the root? The "Deploy to Cloudflare"
# button turns every line of a root .dev.vars.example into a REQUIRED form
# field that blocks the deploy when left blank — and every one of these is
# optional (each connects in-app after deploy). Keep it out of the root.
#
# Everything here is OPTIONAL — the app works by hand with none of it, and each
# of these can be pasted in the app instead (Settings).

# Google Calendar sync + Gmail trip parsing
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""
GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=""
GOOGLE_CALENDAR_ID="primary"

# Gmail confirmation-email parsing into trip segments (uses Claude)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# Calendly (optional ingestion source)
CALENDLY_TOKEN=""
